<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's supreme leader has ruled that the country's stockpile of sixty-percent enriched uranium will stay on Iranian soil, rejecting the central American demand in talks that follow this year's US and Israeli strikes.</s> <s>The directive frames sovereignty over fissile material as non-negotiable, even as Tehran's chief negotiator warns the ceasefire may itself be a tactical pause.</s> <s>What's being called peace talks sits on top of an active war — and the war's terms haven't been settled.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>President Zelenskyy says Kyiv has intelligence on five Russian attack scenarios routed through Belarus, and Ukraine's reinforcing the Chernihiv-Kyiv direction in response.</s> <s>Russia and Belarus have begun joint nuclear drills, and Minsk's accepted deployment of Russian Oreshnik missiles, pulling Lukashenko's autonomy further into Moscow's orbit.</s> <s>After one thousand five hundred forty-eight days of war, a new northern front is opening even as Ukrainian strikes hammer Russia's oil refineries.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>US immigration authorities have arrested Adys Lastres Morera, sister of the head of Cuba's military-run conglomerate <sub alias="GAY-sah">GAESA</sub>, on charges of managing Florida real estate while aiding Havana.</s> <s>GAESA controls roughly forty percent of the Cuban economy — its hotels, dollar stores, and remittance flows are the island's main hard-currency engine.</s> <s>Washington's now mapping the family tier of the conglomerate's offshore network, escalating the financial siege from banks to bloodlines.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The US Treasury has sanctioned nine Lebanese officials accused of embedding Hezbollah inside state institutions, including two sitting lawmakers, the head of the security directorate, and a brigadier general.</s> <s>It's the first American package that names uniformed officers and parliamentarians, not just bank facilitators.</s> <s>Any Lebanese counterparty doing business with those institutions now faces secondary-sanctions risk, accelerating the parallel-economy split the country's been sliding into since two thousand nineteen.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Roughly four million Chinese secondary-vocational students each year must complete mandatory factory internships to earn their diplomas, and some are sent into hazardous industrial worksites with no legal exemption.</s> <s>Schools are paid per student-hour, factories receive sub-minimum-wage labour, and the labour inspectorate can't intervene because the work isn't classified as employment.</s> <s>The supply chains Western brands audit for child labour route through the one channel the audits don't cover.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Aden, a one-hundred-sixty-year-old Hindu temple built for Gujarati traders has survived Yemen's civil war intact, guarded alone by seventy-year-old Abdul Jalil since the building closed in two thousand fifteen.</s> <s>The temple's a relic of an Indian Ocean trading world that once tied Yemeni ports to Gujarat, Zanzibar, and Bombay.</s> <s>Jalil says if he ever leaves, the temple will be looted brick by brick.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's Alaoji power plant is back online after a three-year shutdown, restoring four hundred fifty megawatts to a national grid that loses more capacity to disputes than to demand.</s> <s>The Niger Delta Power Holding Company cleared TotalEnergies debts from a metering quarrel that had blocked gas supply since two thousand twenty-three.</s> <s>Three hundred seventy-five megawatts are now dispatchable, and the company says Alaoji could eventually scale to one thousand one hundred megawatts, in sha'Allah.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two hundred seventy-four climbers summited Mount Everest in a single day this season, a record that coincided with Kami Rita Sherpa's thirty-second ascent and Lhakpa Sherpa's eleventh, the female record.</s> <s>Nepal issued four hundred ninety-four permits at fifteen thousand dollars each, while China kept the northern route closed.</s> <s>The crowding economy on the world's highest mountain has become one of Nepal's most reliable seasonal revenues — and one of its most deadly exports.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>AT and T has sued the state of California to end its carrier-of-last-resort obligation, the rule that forces the company to provide landline service to every potential customer.</s> <s>Around forty thousand low-income Californians depend on those copper lines, often in rural areas where cellular coverage is patchy.</s> <s>The Federal Communications Commission must now decide whether national authority preempts state telecom rules — a fight that could outlast the wires themselves.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Fossils from Canada's Mackenzie Mountains have pushed the origin of animal sexual reproduction back by seven million years, to five hundred sixty-seven million years ago.</s> <s>The same site preserves the earliest traces of animal locomotion — gametes and trackways from one rock layer, recovered by researchers reporting in Science Advances.</s> <s>The textbook timeline for when animals started moving and mating the way modern animals do is older than scholars believed, and the textbooks will move.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The James Webb Space Telescope has mapped morning clouds and clear evenings on a gas giant six hundred ninety light-years away, the first spatially resolved atmospheric map of any exoplanet.</s> <s>A Johns Hopkins team split the transit signal into morning and evening spectra, separating a dayside of vaporised silicates from a cooler condensing nightside.</s> <s>Exoplanet astronomy's crossed from asking whether atmospheres exist to mapping their weather.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Volunteers near Damascus are reviving Syrian crop varieties that vanished during the war, drawing on seeds the regional gene bank evacuated to Morocco and Lebanon in two thousand twelve.</s> <s>The Fertile Crescent collection — wheat, lentil, and barley landraces selected over thousands of years — was Syria's most quietly catastrophic war loss.</s> <s>The Jaramana project runs entirely on volunteer labour, restoring a food sovereignty that no ministry currently funds.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's Chenab River rose by three metres after India opened the Salal Dam upstream, prompting Sialkot authorities to activate emergency flood controls.</s> <s>India suspended the Indus Waters Treaty earlier this year, ending the mandatory advance notification that had governed cross-border releases since nineteen sixty.</s> <s>Silt-flushing continues through the end of May and downstream warnings are now ad hoc — a regional water regime older than most of South Asia's borders is unwinding in real time.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The US cyber agency CISA has opened its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalogue to outside nominations from researchers and vendors.</s> <s>That list triggers mandatory patch deadlines across all federal civilian agencies, and until now the input was internal telemetry plus vendor disclosure.</s> <s>Active-exploitation evidence gathered anywhere in the world can now compel the American federal footprint to act — the post-SolarWinds shift toward externalised vulnerability prioritisation just took its largest public step.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The European Consumer Organisation has filed formal complaints against Google, Meta, and TikTok over scam advertisements, after consumer groups across twenty-seven European countries documented around nine hundred fraudulent ads in four months.</s> <s>The platforms removed roughly twenty-seven percent.</s> <s>Under the Digital Services Act, fines can reach six percent of global turnover — giving Brussels its sharpest financial lever yet over advertising-driven business models.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Universal Music Group has agreed to license artificial-intelligence-generated covers to Spotify — the same kind of output it's currently suing the company Suno over for training on its catalogue.</s> <s>The deal would give Universal a revenue share on synthetic versions of songs by its own artists.</s> <s>Sony and Warner haven't joined, and no pricing or launch date was announced — but the world's largest music label has now drawn the line between unauthorised training and licensed output.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>